{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777790234,"nonce":"/qdfGx725/Kka3pRsyRq0n1Ypd4=","title":"Outreach: cultural mirror to git.sdf.org + SDF member page","message":"Mirror GW-BASIC 2026 to git.sdf.org as part of the SDF preservation-project umbrella. SDF members are the exact audience: long-time Unix users with deep BASIC nostalgia (BSD/Linux/older Unix all shipped BASIC interpreters into the 90s).\n\nThis issue is a bundled effort with the matching UC2 outreach issue (UC2 7cbbf97-equivalent 'Outreach: cultural mirror to git.sdf.org + SDF member page'). The SDF MetaARPA upgrade and member-page setup is one-time work that amortizes across UC2, GW-BASIC 2026, freeclaw, and any future preservation projects.\n\nSteps (shared with UC2):\n1. Upgrade SDF account from ARPA to MetaARPA ($44/yr). Bundles GW-BASIC + UC2 + freeclaw + any future projects + IRC proxy + screen + SSL + NNTP posting.\n2. Create git.sdf.org/evv/gw-basic-2026 mirror; add as 'sdf' remote.\n3. Add to SDF member page (member.sdf.org/~evv) under 'Preservation Projects'.\n4. Add 'Mirrors' section to README listing GitHub (primary), git.sdf.org (cultural), Software Heritage (institutional).\n5. Bonus: bboard announcement on SDF — small audience, perfectly aligned, free.\n\nThis issue is bundled-low-priority on its own; promotes to medium if MetaARPA is acquired for any of the bundled projects.","files":null}]}